{#
  Arm E — NEGATIVE CONTROL.

  Random memories from OTHER questions, count-matched to the Arm A condition so
  that only the CONTENT differs. If this arm does not collapse, the pipeline is
  broken and every other number is suspect.

  PRD §G5 / §R4.3: Arm E runs FIRST in any smoke test, and the pass threshold is
  a NUMBER — never "far below" — set from the P5 pilot and recorded here once
  measured. A threshold that is not a number cannot be failed.

  The prompt is byte-identical to Arm A's. If the control's template differed
  from the treatment's, a collapse could be attributed to the template rather
  than to the absence of evidence.
#}
system: |
  You are answering a question about a conversation history. Use ONLY the
  numbered memories provided. If the memories do not contain the answer, say so
  plainly rather than guessing.

user: |
  {{ memories }}

  Question: {{ question }}

  Answer with the shortest span that answers the question. Do not explain.

control:
  match: count
  source: other_questions
  seed: 20261012
  exclude_gold: true
  exclude_overlap_with_target_question: true

  # THRESHOLDS SET 2026-10-13. See `Research/context/24_open_decisions.md` D5.
  #
  # These two numbers are NOT the same kind of number, and that is the reason they
  # differ by an order of magnitude.
  #
  # RECALL — a LEAK DETECTOR, not a performance bar.
  #   recall@K asks whether a gold SESSION is among the rendered memories. Arm E's
  #   memories are drawn from other questions with gold excluded, so this is 0 by
  #   CONSTRUCTION: it is set overlap and does not care what the model says.
  #
  #   Verified that this does not leak: sessions ARE shared across haystacks (756
  #   of 8,732 distinct sessions across 200 S questions appear in more than one),
  #   so the question was real — but 0/199 other S questions and 0/79 other M
  #   questions held a session that is gold for q0. Shared sessions are shared
  #   DISTRACTORS; gold ids are question-scoped (`answer_280352e9`).
  #
  #   So 0.01 means "essentially zero". Any non-zero recall is a leak and must fail
  #   the gate loudly.
  pass_threshold_recall_below: 0.01

  # ACCURACY — the genuine judgement call, because it will NOT be zero.
  #   Two reasons: a ~9B model has parametric knowledge of some answers, and
  #   token-F1 gives partial credit for overlapping tokens. So 0 is unreachable
  #   and a threshold of 0 would be a gate that cannot pass.
  #
  #   Set A PRIORI, not from a pilot. A gate tuned on the data it is gating is not
  #   a gate. Chosen to sit well above genuine parametric knowledge and well below
  #   a pipeline that ignores context entirely — the latter scores near Arm A's
  #   0.4-0.6 on this benchmark, so 0.15 fires with a wide margin either way.
  #
  #   It is a DETECTOR, not a target. The sweep needs it to catch a broken
  #   pipeline; it does not need to be tight.
  pass_threshold_accuracy_below: 0.15
